{
  "summary": "PyMicroglia now has one Cell grid interface for traces and installed Circadian Workbench single-trace analyses. Registry-driven analysis controls share cell selection, preprocessing, layout and export helpers. Existing CD68, RBM3 and CRY1 experimental grids remain linked.",
  "explanation": "Cell selection and recording-clock binding live in PyMicroglia. Circadian Workbench owns scientific calls, native figure definitions and vector drawing. Missing observations remain missing, unsupported cells retain visible reasons, and exports retain plotted values, native results, run records and replay scripts. Cohort, spatial and experimental-design workflows remain separate because they cannot be interpreted as an independent analysis of one cell trace. The canonical grid defaults to raw total light, a strict centered three-frame mean and robust linear detrending. Trace grids and native grids share layout and input helpers; compatible numeric wavelet views share one spectrum per cell. Legacy calls preserve their defaults. Live controls submit only the selected analysis settings and jobs report computation, drawing and saving progress.",
